            {
                "entry_id": "67a0967d-32f9-347f-88a6-76bf0ff7b3a7",
                "word": "apodictique",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ec389ac5-44e5-4530-bf4e-b1f800f49ee4",
                        "entry_id": "67a0967d-32f9-347f-88a6-76bf0ff7b3a7",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural",
                            "masculine",
                            "feminine"
                        ],
                        "form": "apodictiques"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                        "entry_id": "67a0967d-32f9-347f-88a6-76bf0ff7b3a7",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qui est démonstratif, évident."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "237f12e0-de40-49c7-84ee-2f757d979bcc",
                                "sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                                "text": "Un jugement apodictique présente un caractère d’universalité et de nécessité absolue."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f64a3c5-1238-42e3-9d54-76c2867b077c",
                                "sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                                "text": "Le caractère « apodictique » de la modalité du jugement consiste en ce que celui-ci est affirmé « comme lié de façon indissociable à l’entendement », et, en cela même, comme « nécessaire » et a priori."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4744e442-ad05-410e-a59c-132fac0c1cd1",
                                "sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                                "text": "Le caractère abstrait de la langue, les formes presque mathématiques du style ancien, sont singulièrement favorables, chez Confucius et ses disciples, à l’expression nue et tranchée de l’obligation morale, proclamée dans sa rigueur impérative ou apodictique, pour parler le langage de Kant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "835676a4-48f7-4293-b98d-abab323f60b7",
                                "sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                                "text": "Mes rêves devinrent une certitude, comprenez moi bien : une certitude apodictique, une certitude démontrable, réelle, et ma vie quotidienne devint un rêve."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b0a2dddf-3e91-4e90-90f7-c46f3c7fdc20",
                        "source_entry_id": "67a0967d-32f9-347f-88a6-76bf0ff7b3a7",
                        "source_sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Philosophie) Qui est démonstratif, évident",
                        "target_lang_word": "apodiktisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "apodiktisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fea4a901-cb78-3dba-95cb-0db1d342af36",
                                        "entry_id": "a9cd8025-9c3c-3260-a98d-5dd512651d5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "keinen Widerspruch zulassend"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5921797e-f7cb-4eaf-8bb9-6c2bdeb3fa09",
                                                "sense_id": "fea4a901-cb78-3dba-95cb-0db1d342af36",
                                                "text": "Er behauptete in apodiktischer Form, dass nur sein Vorschlag zum Ziel führe."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09cd889e-e7c5-3b1e-9572-0f376f5bcbc1",
                                        "entry_id": "a9cd8025-9c3c-3260-a98d-5dd512651d5f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "nicht widerlegbar"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4da52499-6dd4-42ce-9d2f-802e436fc584",
                                                "sense_id": "09cd889e-e7c5-3b1e-9572-0f376f5bcbc1",
                                                "text": "Was uns hier gemeiniglich glauben macht, als läge das Prädikat solcher apodiktischen Urteile schon in unserem Begriffe, und das Urteil sei also analytisch, ist bloß die Zweideutigkeit des Ausdrucks."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b971f70e-ccfe-4f28-86a1-945e45fee7a5",
                        "source_entry_id": "67a0967d-32f9-347f-88a6-76bf0ff7b3a7",
                        "source_sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Philosophie) Qui est démonstratif, évident",
                        "target_lang_word": "apodictic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "apodictic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6e2ba632-488d-3d93-a7b1-8a754a81e236",
                                        "entry_id": "66adced5-6a7d-3bab-b5a2-22c35d369eae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Incontrovertible; demonstrably true or certain."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b787f51-18e8-45ca-9ffa-b04cd052f32c",
                                                "sense_id": "6e2ba632-488d-3d93-a7b1-8a754a81e236",
                                                "text": "No religion has ever yet owed its prevalence to ‘apodictic certainty’."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6660fd2-cf6e-4138-95a1-cadfd2912676",
                                                "sense_id": "6e2ba632-488d-3d93-a7b1-8a754a81e236",
                                                "text": "The orca spoke in the odd grammatical tense used either to describe dreams, or to make statements so true they were apodictic, such as \"All things die\" or \"Before my conception I did not exist.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6a17a7f6-995e-3ae5-b373-72b3e33049ce",
                                        "entry_id": "66adced5-6a7d-3bab-b5a2-22c35d369eae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Being a style of argument in which a person presents their reasoning as categorically true, even if it is not necessarily so."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d754bd79-e850-4420-aa26-f719a576d366",
                                                "sense_id": "6a17a7f6-995e-3ae5-b373-72b3e33049ce",
                                                "text": "Don’t be so apodictic! You haven’t considered several facets of the question."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "28213775-3d52-31c5-bba8-105e8f472aa9",
                                        "entry_id": "66adced5-6a7d-3bab-b5a2-22c35d369eae",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Absolute and without explanation, as in a command from God like \\\"Thou shalt not kill!\\"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d85c1755-d749-40d0-a43d-ba1d1b3c976f",
                        "source_entry_id": "67a0967d-32f9-347f-88a6-76bf0ff7b3a7",
                        "source_sense_id": "7e80aa24-abd6-3b62-9930-d4338a42f3f9",
                        "source_sense_description": "(Philosophie) Qui est démonstratif, évident",
                        "target_lang_word": "apodíctico",
